method.description:
The value sampled for the sensor [param name] before the current step, or [param default] when nothing sampled it. Read the world through this in your step, so a misprediction can be blamed on the world.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    entity.prediction.sensors[&"ground"] = _sample_ground

func _network_tick(delta: float, tick: int, fresh: bool) -> void:
    var ground: Dictionary = entity.prediction.sensor(&"ground", {})
[/codeblock]

members.member:
Guesses the input of an entity this peer simulates but does not control, through [member NetwEntity.simulation]. The real input relayed from its controller replaces the guess.
It is called as [code](entity: NetwEntity, tick: int)[/code] and returns a [Dictionary] of input values. Missing values are zero.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    entity.prediction.predict_commands = func(_e, _tick): return {&"throttle": 1.0}
[/codeblock]

signal.description:
Emitted when a predicted tick disagrees with the server, with what the disagreement is blamed on. It is emitted whether or not a correction follows.
[codeblock]
entity.prediction.divergence_detected.connect(
    func(entry: int, attribution: NetwPredict.Attribution):
        if attribution == NetwPredict.ATTRIBUTION_CLOSURE:
            push_warning("transition %d diverged" % entry)
)
[/codeblock]
